<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Banjarmasin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Banjarmasin is a city in South Kalimantan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/martapura">Martapura</a> and Barito rivers near the south coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borneo">Borneo</a>. It was the capital of the Banjar Sultanate, founded in the early sixteenth century, and a port for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a> and forest products. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> annexed the sultanate in 1860 after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banjarmasin-war">Banjarmasin War</a>. Known as the city of a thousand rivers, it is famous for its floating markets.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/banjarmasin.jpg" alt="Banjarmasin" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Halim Drone · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kota_Banjarmasin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
